id: pm-9stazf
title: "pm comments write response replays the entire accumulated history, so one append can emit hundreds of comments"
description: "Appending a comment with pm comments <id> <text> returns the full comments collection instead of a bounded mutation receipt or only the appended entry. On the long-lived release-health item pm-7zs0, a single 2026-08-04 evidence append replayed hundreds of historical comments and dominated a 100k-token command batch. The read-side --limit contract does not protect the write response. This is a distinct CLI/SDK output-contract gap from the closed MCP read issue pm-6vfg."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-04T09:19:57.972Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T14:58:53.291Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-07T14:58:52.797Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-07T14:58:52.797Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "comments, notes, and learnings writes return a bounded shared SDK mutation receipt by default.; Explicit full-history opt-in preserves current inspection capability and emits omission receipts otherwise.; A long-lived fixture proves output size is independent of prior annotation count within the declared token budget.; CLI, SDK, MCP, schemas, docs, and completion contracts remain aligned."
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "pm CLI 2026.8.4 on the 2,310-item dogfood repository"
repro_steps: Run pm comments pm-7zs0 with one new evidence string and inspect stdout; the response enumerates the complete historical comments array.
resolution: "Annotation writes now return the changed entry plus bounded mutation and omission receipts by default, with explicit --full-history/fullHistory/full opt-in across CLI, SDK, and MCP."
expected_result: "Appending or deleting comments, notes, and learnings has output cost independent of accumulated history unless full history is explicitly requested."
actual_result: "Shared annotation primitives, CLI extraction, completion, MCP normalization, schemas, and parity tests pass all exact-head gates."
customer_impact: "Agents spend context tokens re-reading immutable history on every evidence append, directly opposing token-efficient project context management."
