comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T09:20:13.455Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-04: searched every status for comments mutation output, full accumulated comment history, append response token bloat, bounded latest-comment receipt, and annotation output budgets. Closed pm-6vfg fixed the MCP read path; open pm-5t33or owns universal output ceilings; closed annotation-stack items cover input and deduplication. No active or terminal item owns the CLI and shared-SDK write-response projection that reproduced on pm-7zs0."
  "2026-08-07T11:23:42.607Z","harness:claude-code","Same defect confirmed on the notes surface, not only comments, at 2026.8.7 on 2026-08-07: `pm notes <id> --add` replayed the entire accumulated note stream in its write response — 43KB for a single append on an item carrying 15 notes. Scope note for the fix: the replay is a property of the annotation write envelope, so comments, notes and learnings should be corrected together rather than one at a time. Workaround that works today is --quiet."
  "2026-08-07T14:58:04.280Z","harness:codex","Final evidence: comments/notes/learnings share one bounded SDK primitive; default mutations return one changed entry with total_count, returned_count, has_more, mutation_receipt, and omission_receipt. --full-history, SDK fullHistory, and MCP full restore the complete history. Contract snapshots, completion, package surface, and focused/integration tests all pass within the exact 100/100/100/100 suite."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T14:58:04.706Z","harness:codex","Mutation output must describe both what changed and what was deliberately withheld. A bounded receipt is safer for agents than replaying an unbounded collection, while an explicit full-history opt-in preserves lossless workflows."
